# a yes/no is the int 0 or 1 underneath: any operator but equality takes it as that int; of two yes/no values an
# operator that gives 0 or 1 again gives yes/no (notes/bool_type.md, user 2026-11-02, card surprised-simple-implement)
'yes xor no'	yes
'no xor yes'	yes
'yes xor yes'	no
'no xor no'	no
'a = 3 > 2; b = 1 > 2; a xor b'	yes
'yes & no'	no
'yes | no'	yes
'yes + yes'	2
'yes + 1'	2
'no < yes'	yes
'5 xor 3'	6
